$\begin{align}
\left(9^2\right)^{5}&=9^{2\cdot 5}
\\\\
&=9^{10}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $\left(x^m\right)^{n}=x^{m\cdot n}$.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
\left(9^2\right)^{5}&=\underbrace{9^2\cdot 9^2\cdot 9^2\cdot 9^2\cdot 9^2}_\text{5 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{
\underbrace{9\cdot 9}_\text{2 times}
\cdot \underbrace{9\cdot 9}_\text{2 times}
\cdot \underbrace{9\cdot 9}_\text{2 times}
\cdot \underbrace{9\cdot 9}_\text{2 times}
\cdot \underbrace{9\cdot 9}_\text{2 times}}
_\text{5 times}
\\\\
&=9^{10}
\end{align}$
